{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/784761-homebrew-kiths","id":784761,"title":"Homebrew Kiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-12T08:20:38-08:00","id":784761,"title":"Homebrew Kiths","content":"So with the Kickstarter up, I was thinking that now would be a good time for us to place our ideas for homebrewing new kiths. you don't need to put up mechanics, though if you want to that's awesome. Here's one of mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bean Sidhe<br /> <br /> <br /> (I know there is already a Bean Sidhe in the game but I wanted to make it a playable version)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Distant cousins to the fae nobles, The Bean Sidhe are creatures that have fallen from the lofty privilege of their fellows and are now intimately tied to death. Cursed long ago after some unknown tragression this sidhe house was cast from the ranks of nobility to make remind mortals of their own mortality.<br /> <br /> Image: superficially resembling sidhe, the bean sidhe resemble those who have recently died. their skin becomes pale or with or deepest black like all the blood has settled to the surface. despite this they never look grotesque or decayed. their ears are pointed like a sidhe's but their eyes are always completely white.<br /> <br /> Affinity: Actor<br /> <br /> Birthrights: <br /> <br /> <b>Death Sense</b>: The bean sidhe are attuned to the ebb and flow of a life force of the mortal body. With a Perception + Medicine roll difficulty 6, the bean sidhe can sense when their natural death is near. Murder and violence are a shock to the bean sidhe as such actions are the work of free will rather than the Dan, they cannot detect it until after the fact. Loved ones and intimates are eaiser to sense and the Storyteller may lower the difficulty to a minimum of 3 depending on the closeness of the relationship. For the those the bean sidhe are especially close with distance is not a factor. this functions normally in the presence of mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Wailing Keen</b>: The signature move of the bean sidhe, the bean sidhe screams at the top of their lungs and fills the air with the dreadful knowledge of inevitable death. Other fae and the enchanted feel the magic coursing through the song. The bean sidhe makes a Charisma + Performance roll, each success increases the difficulty of the next action of all who hear the bean sidhe by one per success to a maximum of three. the bean sidhe can use this of their own free will (see frailty below) for a point of Glamour. this birthright does not function in the presence of mortals unless the changeling calls upon the wyrd, all mortals hear is loud and somewhat annoying scream.<br /> <br /> <br /> Frailty: <b>Curse of Prophecy</b><br /> <br /> The bean sidhe has little to no control of their birthrights. Death Sense happens reflexively regardless of whether or not the bean sidhe wants it too or not. the storyteller has the right to call on their birthright at all times. If they successfully detect that death is near (with in 48 hours). they must make a willpower roll difficulty 8 or use Wailing Keen. They do not need to spend Glamour to use this power unless they wish to do so of their own free will. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}